WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.934
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:04.334
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:05.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
You made it.

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:09.133
Hey! Let's get to some news.

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:10.667
Guys, today at The White House,
President Biden hosted

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:14.000
the leaders of
Sweden and Finland to discuss

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.567
their applications to join NATO.

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:20.367
Yeah. I didn't know there was an
application process.

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:21.767
The Swedish prime minister
was like,

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:22.901
"Yeah, we have letter of

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:27.067
recommendation from
Norway and ABBA."

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:28.968
During the meeting, Biden told
them that joining NATO

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:31.801
is a complex process
that can get frustrating.

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:34.133
And Sweden said,
"Yeah, we invented IKEA.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:37.434
So we get it. We get it."

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:39.434
That's right -- Biden hosted
Sweden's prime minister,

00:00:39.434 --> 00:00:40.767
and he really went
all out of his way to

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:42.667
make them feel good
and feel at home.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:43.934
But I think he went
a little too far.

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:45.601
-Really?
-Yeah. Listen to this.

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:47.767
[ Swedish Chef
speaking gibberish ]

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:48.901
-That's right.

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:50.868
I think that -- That's too much.

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:53.000
-That's the Swedish Chef, yeah.
-That's too much, right?

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.467
That's --
-Yeah.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.334
-Some business news.

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:59.067
It's been a rough couple of
months for the economy.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:00.367
And I saw that yesterday was

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:04.167
the stock market's worst day
in over two years.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:06.734
Yeah. Stocks fell so fast,

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:09.334
the oxygen masks dropped from
the ceiling at CNBC.

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:11.501
Yeah. It's not good.

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:13.801
Experts say if this keeps up,
every Merrill Lynch office

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:16.200
is going to become
a Spirit Halloween.

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:21.701
Things are so bad,

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:23.634
they replaced the
stock-exchange closing bell

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:25.767
with the losing sound from
"Price is Right."

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:27.767
[ "Price is Right"
losing sound plays ]

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:33.133
That's right -- the stock market
dropped after major retailers,

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:36.033
like Target and Walmart,
reported huge losses.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:39.133
But ones who actually saw their
stock go up by 7% --

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:41.901
this is real -- T.J. Maxx.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:45.300
Yeah.
Yeah, they are crushing it.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.601
They are crushing it,

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:47.734
and you can tell that
they're feeling pretty good.

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:49.167
Watch this.

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:52.701
-Yo! We heard the stock market
is, like, bad or something.

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:53.734
Well, not over here
at T.J. Maxx.

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:54.868
[ Cash register dings ]

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:56.167
We're still flying high,

00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:58.567
thanks to our rock-solid
business strategies like...

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:19.100
So come on down to T.J. Maxx,
where every day is Black Friday.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.133
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:22.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:26.601
Pre-worn.

00:02:26.601 --> 00:02:29.434
-In a size of XXXL
or adult baby.

00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:30.534
-Yeah.

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:31.801
-Guys, get this.

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:33.501
Yesterday, while speaking at
an event in Dallas,

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:36.634
former president George W. Bush
had a pretty major gaffe,

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:38.334
which brings us to
a new segment called

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:40.701
"George W. Bush: Still Got It."

00:02:40.701 --> 00:02:44.167
-The decision of
one man to launch

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:49.000
a wholly unjustified and brutal
invasion of Iraq --

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.000
I mean, of the Ukraine...

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.601
♪♪

00:02:51.601 --> 00:02:54.000
-Still got it!

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.634
-What?!
-Ooh!

00:02:57.634 --> 00:02:59.234
-Wow.

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:02.467
-Well, a lot of people
are graduating this week,

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:04.033
and Father's Day
is around the corner,

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:07.667
so it's officially that
season of dads and grads.

00:03:07.667 --> 00:03:10.534
So, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:10.534 --> 00:03:13.701
What's wrong with that, Tariq?

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:15.367
-Dads and grads?
-Yeah.

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:17.701
-It's so lazy. Come on, now.

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:18.901
-What do you mean?

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:21.400
-They're just combining
two things into one

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.767
so they don't have to, you know,
celebrate both separately.

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.033
It's like telling someone,

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:27.701
"Now here's your Christmas
and birthday present."

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:28.834
It's crap.

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:31.634
-Hmm. Okay. I'm --

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:34.033
-I mean,
why not just celebrate everyone?

00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:38.200
How about, you know, dads
and grads and guys named Brad?

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:43.567
Or dads and grads into bad fads
like being clad in plaid?

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:44.567
It's so sad.

00:03:44.567 --> 00:03:46.200
It makes me mad.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.734
-I mean, it's just two things.
I mean, it's not that --

00:03:48.734 --> 00:03:50.567
-It ain't rad.

00:03:50.567 --> 00:03:54.634
And might I add,
why not dads and grads

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:58.267
and badass lads,
like Josh Gad doing the dab?

00:03:58.267 --> 00:04:00.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.334
Eating crab off an iPad,

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:06.434
drinking Tab in a chem lab,

00:04:06.434 --> 00:04:07.701
reading "People" mag

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:11.200
with Scumbag Chad
no one wants to shag,

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.968
who hates "Downton Ab."

00:04:12.968 --> 00:04:14.334
It's a red flag.

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:16.601
Oh, man, I want to gag.

00:04:16.601 --> 00:04:18.067
-Wow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:23.300
Okay. Well, what do you suggest?

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.033
-Well, we equal
the playing field.

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:27.033
If it's going to be
dads and grads,

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.901
then, next year, it's...

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:31.734
